  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q95-99-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Let $n$ be an integer. Simplify the following.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q95",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\cos(180n^{\\circ}+\\theta)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p17-q95-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "(-1)^n\\cos\\theta",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p17-q95-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Each half-turn reverses the sign of cosine.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Even $n$ adds full revolutions; odd $n$ also adds one half-turn.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos(180n^{\\circ}+\\theta)&=\\begin{cases}\\cos\\theta,&n\\text{ even},\\\\-\\cos\\theta,&n\\text{ odd},\\end{cases}\\\\\\cos(180n^{\\circ}+\\theta)&=(-1)^n\\cos\\theta.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q96",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\tan(180n^{\\circ}+\\theta)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p17-q96-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\tan\\theta",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p17-q96-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Half-turns preserve the gradient and hence tangent.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Full revolutions preserve tangent, and $\\tan(180^{\\circ}+\\theta)=\\tan\\theta$. Both even and odd $n$ therefore give\n$$\\tan(180n^{\\circ}+\\theta)=\\tan\\theta,$$\nwhere tangent is defined.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q97",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\sin(180n^{\\circ}-\\theta)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p17-q97-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "(-1)^{n+1}\\sin\\theta",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p17-q97-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Apply the integer half-turn result to ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "-\\theta",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", then use that sine is odd.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Use the integer half-turn identity $\\sin(180n^{\\circ}+\\theta)=(-1)^n\\sin\\theta$ and $\\sin(-\\theta)=-\\sin\\theta$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin(180n^{\\circ}-\\theta)&=(-1)^n\\sin(-\\theta)\\\\\\sin(180n^{\\circ}-\\theta)&=-(-1)^n\\sin\\theta\\\\\\sin(180n^{\\circ}-\\theta)&=(-1)^{n+1}\\sin\\theta.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q98",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\cos(180n^{\\circ}-\\theta)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p17-q98-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "(-1)^n\\cos\\theta",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p17-q98-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Apply the half-turn result and use that cosine is even.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Apply the cosine half-turn result to $-\\theta$, then use $\\cos(-\\theta)=\\cos\\theta$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos(180n^{\\circ}-\\theta)&=(-1)^n\\cos(-\\theta)\\\\\\cos(180n^{\\circ}-\\theta)&=(-1)^n\\cos\\theta.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q99",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\tan(180n^{\\circ}-\\theta)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p17-q99-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "-\\tan\\theta",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p17-q99-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove the half-turns and use that tangent is odd.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Half-turns preserve tangent. Use $\\tan(-\\theta)=-\\tan\\theta$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan(180n^{\\circ}-\\theta)&=\\tan(-\\theta)\\\\\\tan(180n^{\\circ}-\\theta)&=-\\tan\\theta.\\end{align*}$$\nThese equalities hold where tangent is defined.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      }
    ]
  },
